narrative:
Re : Fraudulent Withdraw Transactions I am demanding a return of funds to my checking account fraudulently withdrawn from my account via an ACH transaction without the approval and required documents for such withdrawals. This fraudulent transaction was made on XX/XX/2024, from my business checking account. 

I have filed claims with Wells Fargo via the phone notification system and received Claim No. XXXX. All pertinent information is detailed in the Claim. 

The entity withdrawing the claim has never been associated with our business nor set up as an ACH approved payee. The two withdrawals on XX/XX/2024 for {$5700.00} and {$3800.00} were represented on Wells Fargo Bank account activity report as follows : XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXXXXXX {$5700.00} XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXXXXXX XXXX XXXX XXXXXXXX XXXX XXXXXXXX XXXX XXXXXXXX {$3800.00}

My mortgage loan was bought by First Horizon Bank, on XX/XX/XXXX, my property taxes are due on XX/XX/XXXX, my escrow account balance was also transferred and it had more than enough to pay the taxes, it seems like the deductions were made but my property taxes were not paid, now im delinquent. 
Property taxes were initially {$2600.00}, now they are {$2900.00} due to penalties, Ive called the mortgage company, and they told me to send an email, I sent an email explaining the situation and demanding for payment, but there has not been an answer and I fear that my house will get a lien .... please help in this situation, what can I do? should I just pay off the property taxes and get straigthen with my bank?, I shouldnt be going through this, the bank should have paid the property taxes from the escrow account on XX/XX/XXXX. 

Total XXXX Taxes Due by XX/XX/XXXX : {$2600.00} Payments applied to XXXX taxes : {$0.00} Total Current Taxes Due : {$2900.00} Prior year ( XXXX ) taxes due ( if any ) : - {$0.00} Total Amount Due For XX/XX/XXXX : {$2900.00}

While on vacation in XXXX and returning back, my fianc ( XXXX XXXX ) and I noticed two charges at XXXX XXXX using his debit card but we were not even in town to make any local purchases. Once we landed from the airport, I contacted my bank and which they told me they would investigate at the time the charges were still pending, but were used on the debit card I had in hand ( not missing ).

We later received a letter, no other contact by phone, email or even on the Wells Fargo App. The letter said based on the information available to them, they found the transactions were authorized and not processed an error, and they were closing the claim. I immediately contacted Wells Fargo back to tell them these in fact were not authorized charges, that as mentioned when I processed the claim we were not even in town to purchase in store purchases at XXXX XXXX in XXXX XXXX, which is where the charges took place. We immediately asked for the debit card to be closed ( even though we had it in hand ). The supervisor that I finally got on the phone told me that there was nothing further they could do for me, so I asked them to send me documentation of this authorization. The supervisor agreed but told me it would be 30 days and there was no way of expediting. The proof to me is Flabbergasting considering I contacted them immediately when this fraud took place and no actions were taken. The charges went through on XX/XX/XXXX and XX/XX/XXXX of 2024 and I am still waiting on proof and it is now XX/XX/XXXX. 
On XX/XX/XXXX {$500.00} was charged and on XX/XX/XXXX {$530.00}
